{
  "$comment": [
    "Single source of truth for Reticulum interface types, read by BOTH the Rust",
    "sidecar (reticulum-sidecar/src/stack/interface_catalog.rs) and the renderer",
    "(src/renderer/lib/reticulum/reticulumInterfaceCatalog.ts).",
    "",
    "configType MUST be one of the type names accepted by the upstream factory",
    "`synthesize_interface` in .rsstack/rsReticulum/crates/rns-runtime/src/interface_factory.rs,",
    "except `BlePeerInterface`, which mesh-client spawns itself from live.rs",
    "(`sync_ble_peer_interfaces`) because upstream has no config type name for it.",
    "",
    "`fields` drives generic form rendering and generic add/edit validation. Types",
    "with bespoke UI (RNode transport selector, presets, BLE picker, host/port) keep",
    "an empty list and their existing hand-written branches; the point of the catalog",
    "is that a NEW type needs no new branch, not that every old one is rewritten.",
    "",
    "A field with no `bind` round-trips through `extra_config`, so it must NOT be",
    "added to KNOWN_IFACE_CONFIG_KEYS in config.rs (same rule as pipe `command`)."
  ],
